Unreleased
----------

- Add a server side: `Fastws_async.Server.accept` answers a WebSocket upgrade
  on a reader and writer (101 with the `Sec-WebSocket-Accept` proof, 426 for a
  version other than 13, 400 for anything else, head bounded to 16 KiB and 100
  lines) and returns the same connection `connect` gives a client;
  `Server.serve` runs a handler per connection on a TCP listener. Subprotocols
  are chosen by a callback; permessage-deflate is not offered. `bin/wsecho` is
  an echo server built on it.
- Never mask a frame written in server mode. A pong built from a client's ping
  kept the ping's masking key and went out masked, which strict clients reject
  with 1002 (RFC 6455 §5.1); this also affected the cryexc server.
- Close timed-out connection attempts and contain late connection errors.
- Reuse zlib streams for `permessage-deflate` connections that negotiate
  `client_no_context_takeover` or `server_no_context_takeover`. This avoids
  destroying and recreating native streams after every WebSocket message.
- Add an offline decompression benchmark covering representative message sizes.
- Fail the connection with 1002 on a frame carrying RSV1 when
  `permessage-deflate` was not negotiated, and on RSV1 riding a control frame
  (RFC 6455 §5.2, RFC 7692 §6.1). Such a frame used to reach the application
  still compressed. Fixes Autobahn case 3.4.
- Rework `bin/wstest` into a full Autobahn client driver: `getCaseCount`, then
  `runCase` per index, then `updateReports`.
